# You design and build LEGO Technic models one step at a time, in a build language.
#
# For each step you write:
# ADD name partnumber color
# CONNECT part.point -> part.point LOCKED|TURNS|STIFF   (points: hole1.., axlehole1.., pin1.., axle1.., clip1..; LOCKED = cross in cross, turn together; TURNS = free; STIFF = friction pin)
# Optional: MESH a.teeth b.teeth / RATIO a b x/y / GROUP g (opens a side build) / END (closes it) / ATTACH g (joins a finished side build into the main model)
# WHY one plain sentence: what this step builds and what it is for.
# A point ending in ~ is an estimate; ? means not known.
#
# Rules: only use real points of each part; a round pin never goes in a cross hole; a shaft that must turn needs round holes; a worm needs stops on both sides; gears must sit at the right distance.
STEP 1
ADD frame-1 32449 lightgray
WHY Starts the build with the thin open frame that both output shafts will be hung from.

STEP 2
ADD pin-1 43093 blue
ADD pin-2 43093 blue
ADD pin-3 43093 blue
ADD pin-4 43093 blue
ADD conn-1 32184 black
ADD conn-2 32184 black
CONNECT pin-1.axle1 -> conn-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT pin-2.axle1 -> conn-1.axlehole2 LOCKED
CONNECT pin-3.axle1 -> conn-2.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT pin-4.axle1 -> conn-2.axlehole2 LOCKED
WHY Builds two pin-and-connector bearing blocks, one for each side of the frame.

STEP 3
CONNECT pin-1.pin1 -> frame-1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT pin-3.pin1 -> frame-1.hole2~ STIFF
WHY Seats the two bearing blocks into the frame's end holes so they stand up ready for the shafts.

STEP 4
ADD diff-1 6573 darkgray
ADD axle-1 4519 lightgray
CONNECT axle-1.axle2 -> diff-1.hole1~ TURNS
WHY Slides the second differential housing onto a free-spinning shaft, leaving both ends of the shaft open for gears.

STEP 5
ADD diff-2 6573 darkgray
ADD bevel-1 6589 tan
CONNECT bevel-1.axlehole1 -> diff-2.bar1? LOCKED
WHY Sets the main differential housing in the middle of the frame and fits its first internal pinion gear onto the housing's cross bar.

STEP 6
ADD axle-2 4519 lightgray
ADD axle-3 4519 lightgray
CONNECT axle-2.axle1 -> diff-2.hole1~ TURNS
CONNECT axle-3.axle1 -> diff-2.hole2~ TURNS
WHY Passes a left and a right output shaft through the housing so each can spin independently of it, like a real differential's axles.

STEP 7
ADD bevel-2 6589 tan
ADD bevel-3 6589 tan
CONNECT bevel-2.axlehole1 -> axle-2.axle2 LOCKED
CONNECT bevel-3.axlehole1 -> axle-3.axle2 LOCKED
WHY Locks a side gear onto each output shaft so they mesh with the housing the way a differential's side gears do.

STEP 8
ADD axle-4 4519 lightgray
CONNECT axle-4.axle1 -> diff-1.hole2~ TURNS
WHY Gives the second housing a shaft on its far side too, so it can carry output gears the same way as the main differential.

STEP 9
ADD spur-1 3648b darkgray
ADD spur-2 3648b darkgray
CONNECT spur-1.axlehole1 -> axle-1.axle1 LOCKED
CONNECT spur-2.axlehole1 -> axle-4.axle2 LOCKED
WHY Locks a 24-tooth gear onto a free end of each of the second housing's shafts, giving it its own pair of outputs.

STEP 10
ADD spur-3 3648b darkgray
ADD spur-4 3648b darkgray
CONNECT spur-3.axlehole1 -> axle-4.axle3 LOCKED
CONNECT spur-4.axlehole1 -> axle-1.axle3 LOCKED
WHY Finishes the model with the last two 24-tooth gears, so both shafts of the second housing drive a matched pair of output gears.
